Vermont: one family enrols for the visual gate, four fail with named obligations\n\nVF25 read all five at the Captain tip, measured all fifteen obligations on each with\nno NOT_MEASURABLE_HERE, and returned nine numeric counters per family.\n\n  vt_seal_nonconviction-set   PASS_COMPLETE_INDEPENDENT  -> BUILT_RASTER_PENDING\n  vt_exp_decriminalized-set   FAIL  KNOWN_PREFILLS\n  vt_seal_18_to_21-set        FAIL  REQUIRED_BEFORE_FILING\n  vt_seal_felony-set          FAIL  REQUIRED_BEFORE_FILING\n  vt_seal_pardon-set          FAIL  REQUIRED_BEFORE_FILING\n\nIt answered the render question I had just put to every live lane, and answered it\nwith a measurement rather than an assurance: pinned 600-00228 page 1 renders\n1,611,695 dark pixels with annotations and 1,602,354 with them hidden, a 9,341-pixel\ngap that is entirely widget /AP /N ink, and the crop of field 16 shows the widget's\nfull 14.4pt frame in the render it used. Two results from inside the read confirm it\nindependently -- the pre-repair erasure came back as REMOVED 1407, which an\nannotation-free render could only have reported as zero, and the fee-waiver pages\ncame back darkDelivered == darkSource at exactly the annotations-on figures. Only\n600-00228 of the five sources carries widget-appearance ink at all; the other four\nprint their boxes as text glyphs. sourceRenderMethod is recorded in all five rows.\n\nFIX130's repair holds, verified per stream rather than by totals. The six surviving\nstroke-only appearances on 600-00228 are byte-for-byte the source widgets' own\n/AP /N /Off, each carrying /MK /BC and /BG and shipping its own /Off -- restore\nclass. All fourteen check boxes on 200-00129 and both on 200-00132A ship /Yes alone\nwith /MK carrying only /CA (4), no /BC, no /BG, no /Off -- remove class, and nothing\nthe court draws was deleted. The 1,407-pixel erasure reproduces exactly on the\npre-repair canonical as one connected component inside field 15's own /Rect, and is\n0 on every page of both current fixtures.\n\nTwo defects no counter saw. vt_exp_decriminalized-set writes eight\nparticipant-identity values onto the fee-waiver form -- name three times, street,\ncity/state/zip, phone, email, and the docket on the Printed Name line of a\ndeclaration made under penalty of perjury -- while its own bound instruction page\nprints 'do not complete or file the fee-waiver form for this petition', while its\nown field map refuses the other 66 fields on that form, and while a sibling family\nrecords the opposite treatment on the identical form. And on the three seal families\nevery disclosure label is the printed caption with the AcroForm field name appended,\nwhile the packet twice says that column is 'the words printed beside the blank';\nfour fields carry two widgets in two unrelated tables, so one identifier names two\ndifferent blanks.\n\nA tool cited in support of an earlier conclusion measures nothing on Vermont:\nscan-inverted-widget-rects.mjs reads source-receipt.json under 'sources' and every\nVermont receipt declares 'documents', so it reports 0 widgets scanned. VF25 measured\ndirectly instead -- 252 widgets across the five pinned sources, 0 inverted. The\nconclusion was right; its evidence was not.\n\nThe three seal families deliver byte-identical canonical and boundary fixtures,\nreproducing the recorded clone group. VF25 declined to convert that into a failed\nobligation because 200-00130 carries no field naming the subsection, and said\nplainly that the only thing distinguishing the three routes reaches the participant\noutside the PDF.\n\nTerminal holds at 192 of 346; every step exit 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T05:05:09Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-da